cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Cerebras SpMV: sparse matrix-vector multiplication on the Cerebras Wafer-Scale Engine"
abstract: >-
  Sparse matrix-vector multiplication (SpMV) for the Cerebras Wafer-Scale
  Engine (WSE-3), written in CSL with a Python host pipeline. The matrix is
  tiled across the processing-element grid and kept resident in on-wafer
  memory, so repeated SpMVs (as in Krylov solvers such as CG) run without
  re-streaming the matrix. Includes the host tiling pipeline, a streaming
  variant for comparison, the benchmark harness used for the reported
  results, and the v2.0 release-candidate measurements (cluster/results/v2.0-data)
  with the notebook that compares v1.0 and v2.0 (analysis/v1_vs_v2.ipynb).
authors:
